\subsection{Comparison under EP3 and Kinetics-600}
Table~\ref{tab:ep3} reports ViT-B/16 results for EP3 and K600. STDD has the highest means: UCF101 85.2 $\pm$ 1.2 against FROSTER (84.8 $\pm$ 1.1) and Open-VCLIP++ (83.9 $\pm$ 0.6), HMDB51 55.9 $\pm$ 0.2 against Open-VCLIP++ (55.6 $\pm$ 1.4), and K600 75.1 $\pm$ 0.7 against FROSTER (74.8 $\pm$ 0.9). Each margin lies within the standard deviation of the baseline it is compared with: 0.4 against FROSTER on UCF101 (std 1.1), 0.3 against Open-VCLIP++ on HMDB51 (std 1.4), and 0.3 against FROSTER on K600 (std 0.9). These results show the best mean rather than a significant improvement.

