\subsection{Semantic Augmentation}
Table~\ref{tab:ep2} compares the text augmentation methods with the same vision backbone. Our spatiotemporal augmentation (ST Aug.) gives 85.2, 55.9 and 75.1 on UCF101, HMDB51 and K600, compared with category text prompts (CT, 83.8, 54.0, 73.5) and spatiotemporal descriptors (STD, 84.9, 55.1, 75.0). The gains over CT are 1.4, 1.9 and 1.6 points. The gain over STD on K600 is 0.1 points, which is within noise. The ST Aug. values match the EP3 row for STDD in Table~\ref{tab:ep3}; the source table does not state its protocol, so we report it as supplied.

