\subsection{Ablation of Space-time Cross Attention}
Table~\ref{tab:ab1} isolates the two STCA operations. Frozen CLIP reaches 74.2 on UCF101 EP3. Prompt-based adaptation reaches up to 82.7 with WSM and continual mixing, and full fine-tuning with MCM alone reaches 84.6. Adding WSM to continual mixing gives the best result, 85.2, an 11.0-point gain over frozen CLIP. Adding WSM to continual mixing improves the result by 2.6 points in the prompt-based setting (80.1 to 82.7) and by 0.6 points in the fully tuned setting (84.6 to 85.2). Continual mixing is slightly better than separate mixing in every row. The table does not include WSM without MCM, so we cannot separate its own contribution.

