\subsection{Text Augmentation and Alignment}
Figure~\ref{fig:ab3} crosses the text prompt types (class names [C], spatial [S], temporal [T], and combinations) with the alignment mechanisms, on UCF101 EP2. For CLIP, spatial prompts give most of the gain over class names, and temporal prompts add little, which is consistent with an object bias in CLIP. For STDD, frame--prompt alignment with [S]+[T] reaches 85.33, compared with 84.62 for [S] alone, a gain of 0.71 points. The video-class variant does not show the same pattern: [S]+[T] gives 85.14, below [S] alone at 85.25. On this panel, the ASKG-based temporal prompts help only in combination with frame-level alignment.

